(Postmortem INC-7157: shipping-api retry storm after a partial outage) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Date: August 2026. Duration: 128 minutes. Severity: SEV2.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Summary) Tj T*
(Customers saw errors from shipping-api for 128 minutes. The trigger was retry storm after a) Tj T*
(partial outage.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Timeline) Tj T*
(09:12 alert fired. 09:20 incident declared. 09:40 mitigation applied.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Root cause) Tj T*
(A change merged two days earlier removed a safety limit, so retry storm after a partial outage) Tj T*
(was able to build up unnoticed until peak traffic. Monitoring did not alert early because the) Tj T*
(threshold was set for the old traffic pattern.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Contributing factors) Tj T*
(- The runbook pointed to a dashboard that had been renamed.) Tj T*
(- The canary stage was skipped for a config-only change.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Action items) Tj T*
(- AI-334: restore the safety limit and add a regression test.) Tj T*
(- AI-941: update the alert threshold to the new traffic pattern.) Tj T*
(- AI-132: never skip the canary, including for config changes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
